@doc """
Standard `Decode` trait declaration.
`Decode<$Format, $To>` converts `Self` into `$To` using a concrete format
marker such as `JsonFormat`.
The `format` and `to` parameters are signature-level TypeRef witness slots and
are not meant to be observed at runtime.
Because `decode(...)` is part of the shared format conversion surface, this
trait is auto-imported when the standard prelude is loaded.

## REPL
xldr(1)> decode("{\"name\":\"surtr\"}", JsonFormat, JsonValue)
Ok(Object(HashMap("name" => String("surtr"))))
"""
@autoimport
deftrait Decode<$Format, $To> {
  # Convert the value into the requested target type for the requested format.
  def decode(self: Self, format: TypeRef<$Format>, to: TypeRef<$To>) -> Result<$To, Error>
}
